                    briefing_text_r1:       `It is 4 March 2026. The EU has just tightened <strong>Ecodesign</strong> (effective in 24 months) and you have lost a <strong>€19M white-label tender</strong> to a rival one energy class higher. Place Alpina Domus on Čater's nexus: where do you sit on <em>green product</em> innovation (efficiency, recyclability) versus <em>green process</em> innovation (clean energy, waste), and is your posture <em>reactive</em> or <em>proactive</em>? Classify the SKU portfolio against the new thresholds (<strong>38% / €83M</strong> at risk), and decide whether the binding constraint is product performance, manufacturing emissions, or brand. Don't forget the <strong>46% white-label volume</strong> — it carries the bigger near-term risk.`,
