                    briefing_text_r2:       `The core decision. Allocate the fixed <strong>€9.0M</strong> across green <em>product</em> innovation (jump energy classes, raise recycled content — high differentiation, slow payback) and green <em>process</em> innovation (on-site solar, heat recovery, waste cuts — cost & emissions, weak customer visibility). Čater's nexus is blunt: the two are <strong>complementary</strong> — all-in on product gives you a green appliance made in a brown, expensive factory; all-in on process improves the plant and leaves nothing visible to sell. Then pick a stance — reactive compliance, <em>selective proactivity</em>, or full leadership — and state the thesis: “we win because…”.`,
