                    insight_advantage:      `Sustainable advantage built: you ran Čater's nexus end to end — a balanced product+process bet channelled through a deliberate environmental strategy, committed with real-options discipline, and protected by a hard-to-imitate capability. Differentiation rose, the factory got cleaner and cheaper, emissions fell, and share grew — an edge the leaders can't copy in two years.`,
                    insight_compliance:     `Compliance receipt: you spent to clear the new thresholds and little more. Every rival will do the same by the same deadline because the regulation forces them to — so in 24 months you're a class behind the leaders and poorer, with an entry ticket where an advantage should be.`,
                    insight_product_only:   `Brown-factory trap: you bought a customer-visible efficiency lead but built it in a high-cost, high-emission plant. The carbon-border rule prices your imported components and a cleaner rival can undercut your price — product gains without process complementarity don't defend margin.`,
                    insight_process_only:   `Invisible-edge trap: you cut Scope-2 and unit cost — genuinely good — but the customer-facing energy label didn't move and the at-risk SKUs still fail. A cost advantage the customer never sees doesn't defend revenue; the marketers had nothing to sell.`,
                    insight_subsidy:        `Subsidy gamble: your process case was built on a 30% subsidy that wasn't enacted, so two-thirds of the tranche went underwater and the cost position suffered. Betting a fixed budget on an un-enacted policy is the classic real-options failure — flexibility, not hope, was the strategy.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed result: parts of the green bet landed, but product, process, policy and defensibility didn't fully reinforce each other — enough seams for the board to doubt whether the edge is durable or just a timing lead.`,
                    insight_imitable:       `The advantage isn't defensible: you never named a valuable, rare and hard-to-imitate capability, so whatever lead you built is a head start the two larger rivals — who out-spend you 3-to-1 — can copy once regulation forces them to follow.`,
                    insight_channel:        `Channel blind spot: you under-weighted the 46% white-label volume, and the dual-sourcing threat put €41M at risk. Optimising the own brand while the partners walked was a portfolio-level miss.`,
                    insight_cliff:          `Still at the cliff: differentiation never climbed far enough to clear the new thresholds convincingly, so the €83M of at-risk revenue stayed exposed and share drifted down.`,
                    insight_costly_green:   `Costly green: you achieved differentiation but unit cost stayed high — a green product made in an expensive factory. The edge is real but the margin is thin, and a cleaner rival can compete on price.`,
                    insight_invisible:      `Invisible green: emissions fell but the customer-visible edge never formed. Cost and Scope-2 are good metrics, but they're not what the customer chooses on — the differentiation the board can sell never materialised.`,

                    hint_compliance:        `You're running a compliance-only pattern — clearing thresholds every rival also clears. Pivot the spend toward a visible differentiation edge that's actually rare.`,
                    hint_product_only:      `Green product, brown factory: differentiation is up but unit cost is rising. Fund the process side — solar and heat recovery — before a cleaner rival undercuts your price.`,
                    hint_process_only:      `Cleaner factory, invisible edge: cost and emissions are good but the customer-facing label hasn't moved. Shift spend to product so there's a differentiation the market can see and pay for.`,
                    hint_subsidy:           `Your case rode on a subsidy that wasn't enacted — the process economics are underwater. Phase or re-scope the tranche so it stands without public money.`,
                    hint_channel:           `You're optimising the own brand while the 46% white-label volume signals dual-sourcing. Defend the channel — €41M is the bigger near-term risk.`,
                    hint_moat:              `Before the board: name what protects the edge. A head start the leaders can copy in two years isn't a sustainable advantage — point to a hard-to-imitate capability.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — differentiation, cost, emissions and share all healthy. Land it: name a hard-to-imitate moat and own the four-KPI scorecard before the board.`,

